y</x:v></x:c><x:c r="D4" s="806" t="str"><x:v>Severity</x:v></x:c><x:c r="E4" s="806" t="str"><x:v>Source Basis</x:v></x:c><x:c r="F4" s="806" t="str"><x:v>Why It Matters</x:v></x:c><x:c r="G4" s="806" t="str"><x:v>Action if No / Unknown</x:v></x:c><x:c r="H4" s="806" t="str"><x:v>Reviewer Note</x:v></x:c></x:row><x:row r="5"><x:c r="A5" s="308" t="str"><x:v>Physical route survey matches current cable schedule / design</x:v></x:c><x:c r="B5" s="808" t="str"><x:v>Unknown</x:v></x:c><x:c r="C5" s="308" t="str"><x:v>All</x:v></x:c><x:c r="D5" s="308" t="str"><x:v>High</x:v></x:c><x:c r="E5" s="308" t="str"><x:v>NECA/NEMA 105; field experience</x:v></x:c><x:c r="F5" s="308" t="str"><x:v>Congestion and undocumented modifications can invalidate calculated loading.</x:v></x:c><x:c r="G5" s="308" t="str"><x:v>Field-verify route, occupancy and support locations before release.</x:v></x:c><x:c r="H5" s="308" t="str" /></x:row><x:row r="6"><x:c r="A6" s="308" t="str"><x:v>Manufacturer-rated support span is not exceeded anywhere</x:v></x:c><x:c r="B6" s="808" t="str"><x:v>Unknown</x:v></x:c><x:c r="C6" s="308" t="str"><x:v>All</x:v></x:c><x:c r="D6" s="308" t="str"><x:v>Critical</x:v></x:c><x:c r="E6" s="308" t="str"><x:v>NEMA metal tray standard; Eaton load/span data</x:v></x:c><x:c r="F6" s="308" t="str"><x:v>Load rating is tied to a tested span.</x:v></x:c><x:c r="G6" s="308" t="str"><x:v>Add supports or obtain verified manufacturer structural data.</x:v></x:c><x:c r="H6" s="308" t="str" /></x:row><x:row r="7"><x:c r="A7" s="308" t="str"><x:v>Supports at fittings / tees / crosses / reducers follow installation guidance</x:v></x:c><x:c r="B7" s="808" t="str"><x:v>Unknown</x:v></x:c><x:c r="C7" s="308" t="str"><x:v>Fittings</x:v></x:c><x:c r="D7" s="308" t="str"><x:v>High</x:v></x:c><x:c r="E7" s="308" t="str"><x:v>NEMA/NECA installation guidance</x:v></x:c><x:c r="F7" s="308" t="str"><x:v>Straight-run support spacing alone is not enough at fittings.</x:v></x:c><x:c r="G7" s="308" t="str"><x:v>Add/relocate supports per approved detail.</x:v></x:c><x:c r="H7" s="308" t="str" /></x:row><x:row r="8"><x:c r="A8" s="308" t="str"><x:v>Expansion joints, anchors and guides are installed per calculated temperature movement</x:v></x:c><x:c r="B8" s="808" t="str"><x:v>Unknown</x:v></x:c><x:c r="C8" s="308" t="str"><x:v>Long / temperature-varying routes</x:v></x:c><x:c r="D8" s="308" t="str"><x:v>High</x:v></x:c><x:c r="E8" s="308" t="str"><x:v>NEMA VE 2 / NECA-NEMA 105</x:v></x:c><x:c r="F8" s="308" t="str"><x:v>Uncontrolled expansion can overload tray, splices and supports.</x:v></x:c><x:c r="G8" s="308" t="str"><x:v>Verify joint locations, anchor/guide arrangement and bonding.</x:v></x:c><x:c r="H8" s="308" t="str" /></x:row><x:row r="9"><x:c r="A9" s="308" t="str"><x:v>Cable bend radius is maintained through tray fittings and dropouts</x:v></x:c><x:c r="B9" s="808" t="str"><x:v>Unknown</x:v></x:c><x:c r="C9" s="308" t="str"><x:v>All</x:v></x:c><x:c r="D9" s="308" t="str"><x:v>High</x:v></x:c><x:c r="E9" s="308" t="str"><x:v>Manufacturer cable data; Southwire installation guide</x:v></x:c><x:c r="F9" s="308" t="str"><x:v>Excessive bending can damage insulation/shields.</x:v></x:c><x:c r="G9" s="308" t="str"><x:v>Correct fitting radius/dropout or cable routing.</x:v></x:c><x:c r="H9" s="308" t="str" /></x:row><x:row r="10"><x:c r="A10" s="308" t="str"><x:v>Single-conductor cables are fastened / cleated for the actual fault duty and formation</x:v></x:c><x:c r="B10" s="808" t="str"><x:v>Unknown</x:v></x:c><x:c r="C10" s="308" t="str"><x:v>Single-conductor power</x:v></x:c><x:c r="D10" s="308" t="str"><x:v>Critical</x:v></x:c><x:c r="E10" s="308" t="str"><x:v>IEC 61914; CMP/cleat test data</x:v></x:c><x:c r="F10" s="308" t="str"><x:v>Short-circuit electrodynamic forces can displace cables violently.</x:v></x:c><x:c r="G10" s="308" t="str"><x:v>Confirm tested cleat family, spacing, hardware and mounting surface.</x:v></x:c><x:c r="H10" s="308" t="str" /></x:row><x:row r="11"><x:c r="A11" s="308" t="str"><x:v>Parallel sets remain grouped/identified consistently through the route</x:v></x:c><x:c r="B11" s="808" t="str"><x:v>Unknown</x:v></x:c><x:c r="C11" s="308" t="str"><x:v>Parallel power sets</x:v></x:c><x:c r="D11" s="308" t="str"><x:v>High</x:v></x:c><x:c r="E11" s="308" t="str"><x:v>NEC installation logic / project layout</x:v></x:c><x:c r="F11" s="308" t="str"><x:v>Unequal geometry can affect current sharing and magnetic forces.</x:v></x:c><x:c r="G11" s="308" t="str"><x:v>Confirm installed grouping/spacing/phase sequence.</x:v></x:c><x:c r="H11" s="308" t="str" /></x:row><x:row r="12"><x:c r="A12" s="308" t="str"><x:v>Grounding / bonding path is electrically continuous across splices and expansion joints</x:v></x:c><x:c r="B12" s="808" t="str"><x:v>Unknown</x:v></x:c><x:c r="C12" s="308" t="str"><x:v>Metallic tray</x:v></x:c><x:c r="D12" s="308" t="str"><x:v>Critical</x:v></x:c><x:c r="E12" s="308" t="str"><x:v>NEC/NECA/NEMA grounding practice</x:v></x:c><x:c r="F12" s="308" t="str"><x:v>Mechanical continuity alone may not satisfy the grounding design.</x:v></x:c><x:c r="G12" s="308" t="str"><x:v>Verify bonding jumpers, EGCs, tray rating and connections.</x:v></x:c><x:c r="H12" s="308" t="str" /></x:row><x:row r="13"><x:c r="A13" s="308" t="str"><x:v>Dissimilar-metal / corrosion controls match the environment</x:v></x:c><x:c r="B13" s="808" t="str"><x:v>Unknown</x:v></x:c><x:c r="C13" s="308" t="str"><x:v>Wet/corrosive locations</x:v></x:c><x:c r="D13" s="308" t="str"><x:v>High</x:v></x:c><x:c r="E13" s="308" t="str"><x:v>Eaton material guidance; corrosion practice</x:v></x:c><x:c r="F13" s="308" t="str"><x:v>Bare Cu/Al contact and wrong finishes can create premature failure.</x:v></x:c><x:c r="G13" s="308" t="str"><x:v>Use approved isolation/insulated conductors/material system.</x:v></x:c><x:c r="H13" s="308" t="str" /></x:row><x:row r="14"><x:c r="A14" s="308" t="str"><x:v>Covers preserve drainage/ventilation and are mechanically secured for environment</x:v></x:c><x:c r="B14" s="808" t="str"><x:v>Unknown</x:v></x:c><x:c r="C14" s="308" t="str"><x:v>Covered tray</x:v></x:c><x:c r="D14" s="308" t="str"><x:v>High</x:v></x:c><x:c r="E14" s="308" t="str"><x:v>NEMA/NECA installation guidance</x:v></x:c><x:c r="F14" s="308" t="str"><x:v>Covers change thermal conditions and can become wind hazards.</x:v></x:c><x:c r="G14" s="308" t="str"><x:v>Verify clamp quantity, drainage and project wind criteria.</x:v></x:c><x:c r="H14" s="308" t="str" /></x:row><x:row r="15"><x:c r="A15" s="308" t="str"><x:v>Fire barriers / penetrations use tested approved configurations</x:v></x:c><x:c r="B15" s="808" t="str"><x:v>Unknown</x:v></x:c><x:c r="C15" s="308" t="str"><x:v>Fire-rated boundaries</x:v></x:c><x:c r="D15" s="308" t="str"><x:v>Critical</x:v></x:c><x:c r="E15" s="308" t="str"><x:v>NRC fire barrier operating experience</x:v></x:c><x:c r="F15" s="308" t="str"><x:v>Unqualified field configurations can fail intended fire endurance.</x:v></x:c><x:c r="G15" s="308" t="str"><x:v>Use tested listed system; resolve deviations through fire protection engineering.</x:v></x:c><x:c r="H15" s="308" t="str" /></x:row><x:row r="16"><x:c r="A16" s="308" t="str"><x:v>Redundant / life-safety / control circuits have required separation</x:v></x:c><x:c r="B16" s="808" t="str"><x:v>Unknown</x:v></x:c><x:c r="C16" s="308" t="str"><x:v>Critical systems</x:v></x:c><x:c r="D16" s="308" t="str"><x:v>Critical</x:v></x:c><x:c r="E16" s="308" t="str"><x:v>NEC/project criteria; NRC fire PRA experience</x:v></x:c><x:c r="F16" s="308" t="str"><x:v>Common-cause fire or physical damage can defeat redundant functions.</x:v></x:c><x:c r="G16" s="308" t="str"><x:v>Verify project separation / barrier criteria.</x:v></x:c><x:c r="H16" s="308" t="str" /></x:row><x:row r="17"><x:c r="A17" s="308" t="str"><x:v>Seismic bracing / support qualification is addressed where project requires it</x:v></x:c><x:c r="B17" s="808" t="str"><x:v>Unknown</x:v></x:c><x:c r="C17" s="308" t="str"><x:v>Seismic projects</x:v></x:c><x:c r="D17" s="308" t="str"><x:v>Critical</x:v></x:c><x:c r="E17" s="308" t="str"><x:v>Seismic cable-tray support research / ASCE/project criteria</x:v></x:c><x:c r="F17" s="308" t="str"><x:v>Tray/support response is system-specific and can be nonlinear.</x:v></x:c><x:c r="G17" s="308" t="str"><x:v>Provide approved seismic design or qualification.</x:v></x:c><x:c r="H17" s="308" t="str" /></x:row><x:row r="18"><x:c r="A18" s="308" t="str"><x:v>Wind / ice / external loads are included where exposed</x:v></x:c><x:c r="B18" s="808" t="str"><x:v>Unknown</x:v></x:c><x:c r="C18" s="308" t="str"><x:v>Outdoor / exposed</x:v></x:c><x:c r="D18" s="308" t="str"><x:v>High</x:v></x:c><x:c r="E18" s="308" t="str"><x:v>ASCE/project criteria; manufacturer guidance</x:v></x:c><x:c r="F18" s="308" t="str"><x:v>Cable load alone is not the only support load.</x:v></x:c><x:c r="G18" s="308" t="str"><x:v>Add project environmental load or approved structural detail.</x:v></x:c><x:c r="H18" s="308" t="str" /></x:row><x:row r="19"><x:c r="A19" s="308" t="str"><x:v>Installed ambient / heat sources are consistent with ampacity design</x:v></x:c><x:c r="B19" s="808" t="str"><x:v>Unknown</x:v></x:c><x:c r="C19" s="308" t="str"><x:v>All power circuits</x:v></x:c><x:c r="D19" s="308" t="str"><x:v>High</x:v></x:c><x:c r="E19" s="308" t="str"><x:v>NEC/IEC ampacity basis</x:v></x:c><x:c r="F19" s="308" t="str"><x:v>Actual thermal environment can invalidate ampacity.</x:v></x:c><x:c r="G19" s="308" t="str"><x:v>Recalculate using field ambient/heat source conditions.</x:v></x:c><x:c r="H19" s="308" t="str" /></x:row><x:row r="20"><x:c r="A20" s="308" t="str"><x:v>Cable pulling limits, bend radii and sidewall pressure were checked for difficult pulls</x:v></x:c><x:c r="B20" s="808" t="str"><x:v>Unknown</x:v></x:c><x:c r="C20" s="308" t="str"><x:v>Long/heavy/duct pulls</x:v></x:c><x:c r="D20" s="308" t="str"><